<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kayah State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kayah State is the smallest state of Myanmar, in the hills of the east bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, with its capital at Loikaw. It was formed from the former Karenni States, which joined the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> in 1948, and was renamed Kayah State in 1952. Armed Karenni groups have fought the central government there for much of the period since independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kayah-state.jpg" alt="Kayah State" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saosukham · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Htee_Zai_Kha_Waterfall_border_of_Shan_and_Kayar_State_(4).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
